    "rawMarkdown": "I suggest you don't download it locally unless you plan to train locally. What I did was to have a script aggregate all non-pixel data (csv) in a Kaggle notebook and download it as a zip file. it is quite small I think, just a couple of GB max. AND for pixel data, download just a couple of studies to help you understand what's going on.",
    "content": "<p>I suggest you don't download it locally unless you plan to train locally. What I did was to have a script aggregate all non-pixel data (csv) in a Kaggle notebook and download it as a zip file. it is quite small I think, just a couple of GB max. AND for pixel data, download just a couple of studies to help you understand what's going on.</p>",
